This product includes software developed by ApodexAI
(https://github.com/ApodexAI/FrontierAgent), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

Portions of the following files are derived from FrontierAgent source and have
been modified. Each file carries the attribution and a description of the
changes in its module docstring:

  agent/finalization_reserve.py
      derived from frontier_agent/components/observers/finalization_reserve.py
      and last_turn_forcer.py (hold back budget to produce an answer; force a
      tool-free final request). Reshaped around Hermes' own documented
      budget-exhaustion grace call rather than an early pressure warning.

  agent/reasoning_runaway.py
      derived from frontier_agent/core/runtime/loop/_runaway.py
      (detecting a reply whose whole output budget went to reasoning, and
      resampling it at a reduced max_tokens). Extended with a tier that reads
      the reasoning fields Hermes' transports already capture.

  agent/text_repetition.py
      derived from frontier_agent/components/observers/text_repetition_guard.py
      (word-bigram shingles + Jaccard similarity across recent assistant
      turns, localised hints, advisory-only by default)

  agent/budget_consistency.py
      derived from frontier_agent/core/runtime/loop/budget_consistency.py
      (startup warnings for token budgets that cannot all hold at once)

  tools/subagent_rescue.py
      derived from workflows/agent_team/subagent_runtime.py::force_final_answer
      and frontier_agent/components/finalization/recovery.py (recovering an
      answer from a subagent that ended without writing one; recording which
      fallback produced it)

  tools/url_safety.py
      pin_to_address / strip_cross_origin_credentials derived from
      plugins/tools/_bounded_fetch.py (dialling an already-validated address
      while preserving the Host header and TLS SNI, so certificate
      verification still fails closed)
